            <title>[LU-21027] lctl dk: raw mode fails with EINVAL for relative file names</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21027</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;"lctl dk &amp;lt;file&amp;gt; 1" (raw mode) fails with an unhelpful error when &amp;lt;file&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
is a relative path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In raw mode, lctl passes the file name unchanged to the kernel&lt;br/&gt;
dump_kernel control file. A relative name is rejected with EINVAL, and&lt;br/&gt;
lctl prints only:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    write(dumpfile) failed: Invalid argument&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An absolute path works. Text mode is not affected, because lctl builds&lt;br/&gt;
its own absolute temporary name (/tmp/lustre-log&amp;lt;time&amp;gt;.&amp;lt;usec&amp;gt;) and&lt;br/&gt;
converts it afterwards.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Steps to reproduce:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    # lctl dk dumpfile 1&lt;br/&gt;
    write(dumpfile) failed: Invalid argument&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    # lctl dk /tmp/dumpfile 1&lt;br/&gt;
    (works; "file /tmp/dumpfile" reports "data")&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Debug prints in jt_dbg_debug_kernel() show that dbg_write_cmd() fails&lt;br/&gt;
with errno 22 when the name is "dumpfile" (8 bytes), and succeeds with&lt;br/&gt;
the absolute name used in text mode.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Expected behavior:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A relative file name works in raw mode, or lctl prints a clear error&lt;br/&gt;
such as "raw mode requires an absolute path".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Why it matters:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raw mode avoids the text conversion and timestamp sort, which are the&lt;br/&gt;
memory-heavy part of "lctl dk". On a node with a small memory cgroup, a&lt;br/&gt;
text dump can push the cgroup over its limit. Raw mode is a useful workaround, but it&lt;br/&gt;
should not require reading the source to use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Proposed fix:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In jt_dbg_debug_kernel(), build an absolute path with getcwd() when the&lt;br/&gt;
raw-mode file name is relative, with length checks before concatenation&lt;/p&gt;</description>
